==DE30 LA==
With a reduced bore and stroke at {{convert|88 x 82.1|mm|2|abbr=on}} and reduced compression ratio at 10.7:1, '''DE 30 LA''' is turbocharged with twin [[IHI Corporation|IHI]] turbochargers for {{convert|245|kW|hp PS|0|abbr=on}} at 5,250–6,000rpm and {{convert|480|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque at 1,600–4,000rpm and weighs in at 179.2&nbsp;kg DIN.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.germanboost.com/showthread.php?44145-Best-Mercedes-tuning-value-A-preview-of-the-330-horsepower-Mercedes-M276-DELA-30-Twin-Turbo-3-0-liter-V6-going-into-the-W205-C205-C400|title=Best Mercedes tuning value|website=germanboost.com}} {{dead link|date=December 2023}}</ref> This engine was introduced on 2013 C400(W205), and used for E400 Coupe 4Matic, ML(GLE)400 4Matic, E450 4Matic, CLS450, S450, S500e and other models.

For 2015–2016, a higher output version is also offered with {{convert|362|hp|kW PS|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|384|lbft|Nm|0|abbr=on}} on higher boost and 10.5:1 compression ratio for C450 AMG and GLE450 AMG. This engine powers 2017–on AMG SLC43, AMG C43 and AMG GLE43,<ref>{{cite web|author=Sichao Chen |url=http://youwheel.com/home/2016/01/15/the-demise-of-amg-sport-2017-mercedes-amg-slc43/ |title=The Demise of AMG Sport: 2017 Mercedes-AMG SLC43 &#124; YouWheel - Your Car Expert |publisher=YouWheel |date=2016-01-15 |accessdate=2022-05-17}}</ref> as well as 2018–2020 E450 4Matic,<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.ultimatespecs.com/car-specs/Mercedes-Benz/114199/Mercedes-Benz-E-Class-Estate-(W213)-450-4MATIC.html | title=Mercedes Benz e Class Estate (W213) 450 4MATIC Technical Specs, Dimensions }}</ref> S560e<ref>{{cite web| url = https://www.autocar.co.uk/car-review/mercedes-benz/s-class/first-drives/mercedes-benz-s-class-s560e-2018-review| title = Mercedes-Benz S-Class S560 e plug-in hybrid 2018 review {{!}} Autocar}}</ref> and other models.

For 2018–2021, another higher output version is offered with {{convert|385|hp|kW PS|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|384|lbft|Nm|0|abbr=on}} on higher boost.

